  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 135 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nA large shortwave trof aloft swings through the region today and \nbehind it upper ridging builds in. We have a tight sfc pressure \ngradient today behind last night/this morning's cold front. This is \nleading to breezy northwest winds today with gusts up to around 25 \nmph at times. Significantly cooler temperatures today as well as we \nstruggle to get out of the 50s. Winds are expected to remain breezy \nthrough most of tomorrow along with highs that will likely hover \nright around 60. \n\nSaturday night a potent sfc high slides through and off to the \nnortheast by daybreak Sunday. With clear and calm to nearly calm \nconditions Saturday night, along with dewpoints in the 30s, we will \nlikely see a first frost of the season across most of the CWA as \nlows dip into the 30s. There may even be some brief freezing \ntemperatures in far west portions of the CWA. A Frost Advisory will \nlikely be needed. \n\nWith deep layer ridging in place for a little while, we can expect \ndry conditions and large diurnal temperature swings next week. \nSunday kicks off a warming trend that will bring temperatures back \nup to normal and slightly above normal for mid to late week. Highs \nwill generally be in the 70s and lows will generally be in the\n40s.",
